{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"title":"Early Stopping & Generalization Control","role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","modules":[{"name":"SwiftML"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Halt iterative training dynamically when validation performance ceases to improve to prevent overfitting."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/EarlyStoppingCallbacks"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterative estimators like multi-layer perceptrons ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLPClassifier"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLPRegressor"},{"type":"text","text":") and gradient boosted decision trees ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GradientBoostedTreesRegressor"},{"type":"text","text":") improve their training loss over successive iterations. However, after sufficient capacity has been fit, additional epochs frequently lead to overfitting on training noise and deteriorating generalization on unseen data."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EarlyStopping"},{"type":"text","text":" provides a decoupled, value-type training callback that monitors validation loss or performance metrics across successive epochs, halting training and optionally restoring optimal model weights."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Mechanics & State Machine","anchor":"Mechanics--State-Machine","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["Epoch Evaluation (Score S_t)","            │","            ▼"," Is (Best - S_t) > minDelta?","   ├── YES ──► Reset wait = 0, update bestScore = S_t, checkpoint weights","   └── NO  ──► Increment wait = wait + 1","                 │","            Is wait >= patience?","              ├── YES ──► shou